 "issue": 1420,
 "issue_title": "Bug: validate from_records column names before pandas construction",
 "issue_body": "## Summary\n\n`ArFrame.from_records(..., columns=...)` does not validate the `columns` argument before passing it through pandas/from_pandas. Non-string column labels can be silently converted, and bare strings leak pandas `Index(...)` errors.\n\n## Why it matters\n\n`from_records()` is a public constructor. It should enforce its documented `list[str] | None` contract and provide Arnio-specific messages for invalid column inputs.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `arnio/frame.py::ArFrame.from_records()` accepts `columns: list[str] | None`.\n- The method checks row lengths but does not validate that `columns` is a list/tuple of strings or reject a bare string.\n- `from_pandas()` later converts labels to strings, so `columns=[1]` becomes `\"1\"` silently.\n\n## Reproduction or trigger\n\n```python\nimport arnio as ar\n\nprint(ar.ArFrame.from_records([[1]], columns=[1]).columns)\nar.ArFrame.from_records([[1]], columns=\"a\")\n```\n\nObserved behavior:\n\n```text\ncolumns=[1] -> ['1']\ncolumns=\"a\" -> TypeError from pandas: Index(...) must be called with a collection of some kind\n```\n\n## Expected behavior\n\n`from_records()` should reject invalid column arguments clearly:\n\n```text\nTypeError: columns must be a list or tuple of strings, not a string\nTypeError: columns must contain only strings\n```\n\n## Actual behavior\n\nSome invalid values are converted silently, and others produce pandas-level errors.\n\n## Suggested direction\n\n- Add local validation for `columns` before constructing the pandas DataFrame.\n- Reject bare strings/bytes and non-string items.\n- Add tests for `columns=\"a\"`, `columns=[1]`, valid string columns, and duplicate columns if not already covered.\n\n## References\n\n- `arnio/frame.py`\n- `tests/test_convert.py`\n- `tests/test_from_records.py` if this test file is added later\r\n",
 "issue_url": "https://github.com/im-anishraj/arnio/issues/1420",
 "pr": 1772,
 "pr_title": "Fix from records columns validations",
 "pr_body": "## Summary\r\n\r\nFixes #1420\r\n\r\nAdds explicit validation for `ArFrame.from_records(..., columns=...)`\r\nbefore pandas DataFrame construction.\r\n\r\nThis keeps the public API aligned with the documented\r\n`list[str] | None` contract and prevents pandas-level errors\r\nor silent coercion of invalid column labels.\r\n\r\n## Changes\r\n\r\n- reject bare `str` / `bytes` column inputs\r\n- reject non-list/tuple column containers\r\n- reject non-string column entries\r\n- preserve valid list/tuple behavior\r\n- add focused regression tests\r\n\r\n## Tests\r\n\r\n```bash\r\npy -3.12 -m pytest tests/test_convert.py -k from_records -v",
 "fix_commit": "1e3ce49ff8ef2f7f737ad5801d2b7487aff57891",
